   "stylePrice": 29,
   "group": "website",
   "guide": "<h4>What you get</h4><p>A complete, responsive <b>Car Dealership Website</b> with 3D effects, in one file. Three colour styles are included; pick one. Everything you may want to change lives in two marked blocks at the top of the script: <code>CONFIG</code> (settings) and <code>DATA</code> (texts, cars, prices, hours).</p><h4>1. Open it in 1 minute</h4><ol><li>Choose the style you like and press <b>Copy code</b>.</li><li>Open Notepad (or VS Code), paste, and save the file as <code>index.html</code> (type the name with the .html ending).</li><li>Double-click the file: your website opens in the browser. Nothing to install.</li></ol><h4>2. Make it yours</h4><ul><li><code>CONFIG.brand</code> — your business name.</li><li><code>CONFIG.currency</code> — <code>\"$\"</code>, <code>\"€\"</code>, <code>\"£\"</code> or any symbol.</li><li><code>DATA.hero</code> — the big headline, subtitle and buttons.</li><li><code>DATA.contact</code> and <code>DATA.hours</code> — your address, phone, e-mail and opening hours.</li><li><code>DATA.reviews</code> — replace the sample reviews with real ones (or delete them).</li></ul><h4>3. Add your own cars</h4><p>Each item in <code>DATA.items</code> looks like this:</p><p><code>{ id:\"x1\", name:\"Name\", category:\"Group\", price:10, desc:\"Short text\", emoji:\"⭐\", image:\"photos/x1.jpg\", badge:\"New\" }</code></p><ul><li>Copy a line, change the values, add a comma. Categories become the filter buttons automatically.</li><li><code>image</code> is optional: put a photo link or file name to replace the emoji with a real picture.</li><li>Delete items you do not need. Prices are numbers (no currency symbol).</li></ul><h4>4. Connect YOUR data (no coding)</h4><p><b>Option A — edit the file.</b> Easiest for small catalogues: change <code>DATA.items</code> directly.</p><p><b>Option B — Google Sheet (recommended).</b> Manage your cars in a spreadsheet and the website updates itself:</p><ol><li>Make a Google Sheet. In row 1 write these column names: <code>id, name, category, price, desc, emoji, image, badge, meta</code>. Add one item per row (for several sizes/colours/details separate them with <code>|</code>, e.g. <code>S|M|L</code>).</li><li>Menu: <b>File → Share → Publish to the web</b> → choose your sheet and <b>Comma-separated values (.csv)</b> → <b>Publish</b> → copy the link.</li><li>Paste the link between the quotes in <code>CONFIG.dataUrl</code>. Save and refresh: the website now shows your sheet. Edit the sheet any time; changes appear after a refresh.</li></ol><p><b>Option C — your own server or API.</b> Put a JSON file (a list of items with the same fields) online, or make your API return that list, and paste its address into <code>CONFIG.dataUrl</code>. The website also accepts <code>{ \"items\": [ ... ] }</code>.</p><h4>5. Receive enquiries</h4><p>Visitors press <b>Enquire</b> on an item or use the form at the bottom. Their message arrives on <b>your WhatsApp</b> (<code>CONFIG.whatsapp</code>) or <b>your email</b> (<code>CONFIG.email</code>). For automatic emails use a free <b>Formspree</b> / <b>Getform</b> form and paste its address in <code>CONFIG.formAction</code>.</p><h4>6. Put it online (free)</h4><ol><li>Go to <b>app.netlify.com/drop</b> (or Cloudflare Pages → Upload assets).</li><li>Make a folder, put your <code>index.html</code> (and a <code>photos</code> folder if you use pictures) inside, and drag the folder onto the page.</li><li>You get a live link. Later connect your own domain in the host's settings.</li></ol><h4>7. Good to know</h4><ul><li>This is a front-end website: it needs no server. Carts are saved in the visitor's browser. For stock control, customer accounts or card payments connect a service (Shopify Buy Button, Stripe, Supabase…) — the structure of <code>DATA</code> makes that easy for a developer.</li><li>Colours and fonts are CSS variables at the top of the <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block (<code>--ac</code> is the main colour): change them to re-colour the site.</li><li>Images: use real photos for the best result (JPG/WebP, under 300 KB each).</li></ul>",
   "tagline": "Car inventory with a 3D ring hero, filters and test-drive enquiries.",
